===== corrections
{"id": "C1", "severity": "correct", "criteria": ["successor-01.working.q.stationary-meaning"], "field": "check (last clause) / authority", "finding": "The specialist proposal P1 ('hold a phase of the loop so the switch changes motion, not identity') is written into a requirement-labelled check. PLAR line 422 and BRIEF line 3 do not require the stationary symbol to be a phase of the loop; a new static glyph (P2) would satisfy them and be rejected.", "correction": "Keep the required outcome (Working's own symbol; not success; not pause). Move the phase-identity clause to the expert clause set with scope 'this successor, P1'.", "locators": ["plar-purpose", "brief-activity", "assign-step2"]}

{"id": "C2", "severity": "correct", "criteria": ["successor-01.working.q.stationary-distinct-retry-start", "successor-01.retry.q.retry-meaning-without-color", "successor-01.paused.q.pause-meaning-without-color", "successor-01.delivery.q.distinction"], "field": "authority", "finding": "The authority field says 'requirement' while the basis labels the Start clause an inference. Retry and Start have different authority: Retry distinction is BRIEF line 3 by direct reading; Start distinction is the shared-consumer inference settled as D4.", "correction": "Split the authority per clause: Retry = requirement (brief-retry); Start = inference (view-idle, view-consumers, succ-idle, succ-consumers). Caller answer to the specialist's question 2: adopt both clauses with those labels.", "locators": ["brief-retry", "view-idle", "view-consumers", "succ-idle", "succ-consumers"]}

{"id": "C3", "severity": "clarify", "criteria": ["successor-01.working.q.geometry", "successor-01.working.q.consumers-normal-motion", "successor-01.working.q.reduced-motion-consumer-mapping", "successor-01.retry.q.consumers", "successor-01.paused.q.consumers", "successor-01.delivery.q.destination", "successor-01.working.q.style-coherence", "successor-01.retry.q.style-coherence", "successor-01.paused.q.style-coherence", "successor-01.working.q.stationary-distinct-ready-paused"], "field": "authority / scope", "finding": "The proposal's convention folds owner brief, caller update, assignment process requirements and consumer-code of the PROPOSED successor module into one 'requirement' label. The successor module is itself a revisable design proposal (the proposal's own source role), so descriptor-field clauses (still, holdFrame, animate, motion) bind a design, not an owner outcome; a different mapping (M1) would be rejected by the literal checks while satisfying PLAR line 422 and the assignment.", "correction": "In the corrected proposal, carry per-clause authority classes: owner (BRIEF), caller update (PLAR 422/AUTHORING-UPDATE), assignment (FOCUSED-SUCCESSOR), consumer-code (original module | proposed successor | fixture), measured, expert, inference. Scope successor-specific clauses to 'this successor destination as designed'. No outcome changes.", "locators": ["plar-purpose", "assign-step4", "succ-running", "succ-describe"]}

{"id": "C4", "severity": "clarify", "criteria": ["successor-01.working.q.activity-not-success"], "field": "check / scope", "finding": "The check binds every individual frame while the brief binds the loop; the held frame is bound by the caller update. The basis discloses the extension but the check does not scope it.", "correction": "Scope: loop (owner) and held cell (caller update) are required; transient frames are an expert clause with the stated 100 ms rationale.", "locators": ["brief-activity", "plar-purpose"]}

{"id": "C5", "severity": "clarify", "criteria": ["successor-01.working.q.stationary-cell-identity"], "field": "authority", "finding": "Labelled 'observation', but the first clause chooses cell 0 (specialist proposal P1 bound to the caller's `still: 0` design); only the numbers are observations.", "correction": "Label 'proposal (cell choice) + observation (measurements)'; keep the record and its redo rule.", "locators": ["succ-running", "succ-still-comment"]}

{"id": "C6", "severity": "clarify", "criteria": ["successor-01.working.q.transparent-exterior-measured"], "field": "authority", "finding": "Labelled 'observation', but the construction-scoped rejection clause (alpha == cw^k(seed)) is an expert construction choice.", "correction": "Label the rejection clause 'proposal (seed-rotation construction only)'; keep the flag as diagnostic.", "locators": ["brief-transparent"]}

{"id": "C7", "severity": "note", "criteria": ["successor-01.working.q.stationary-meaning"], "field": "check ('with its consumer label present')", "finding": "The fixture renders the label beside the glyph (view.mjs line 62), but BRIEF line 3 asks for readable silhouettes; the label is viewing context, not a carrier of the required reading.", "correction": "State that the glyph must carry the non-success/non-pause reading by itself; the label may be present as in the consumer.", "locators": ["sv-label", "brief-transparent"]}

{"id": "C8", "severity": "note", "criteria": ["all engine/live and visual criteria"], "field": "evidence status", "finding": "No successor fixture capture exists (render-01 has no render.json; its launch.json root is a different project copy), so every destination/temporal criterion is unevidenced and every visual criterion has only the specialist's preliminary composites. The proposal states this correctly; this review does not convert any of it into a pass.", "correction": "None to the proposal. Production-time work (outside this assignment): run renderer-successor/capture.mjs against this consumer root, run check.py with a baseline, retain the capture, then perform caller viewing of native/enlarged fixture views.", "locators": ["cont-scope", "cont-no-pass", "cap-scope", "sc-scope"]}

{"id": "C9", "severity": "note", "criteria": ["reuse"], "field": "reuse.satisfied_now_by_specialist_measurement", "finding": "Listing geometry, measured-exterior, frame-assembly (reuse case) and cell-identity as satisfied by measurement is correct for mechanical records and was reproduced by the caller. The 'preliminary visual pass' list is correctly labelled not acceptance.", "correction": "None.", "locators": ["state-candidate"]}

{"id": "C10", "severity": "clarify", "criteria": ["successor-01.working.q.consumers-normal-motion", "successor-01.working.q.motion-continuity", "successor-01.delivery.q.continuity"], "field": "check / evidence_route (temporal evidence)", "finding": "Raised by the specialist in round 1 (S5) and verified by the caller against the fixture and checker: the fixture samples each live cell once (view.mjs line 157) and check.py tests that one frame with a boundary tolerance (line 140); 'cycling through all four cells' is asserted only on the synthetic timeline (lines 163-164). The actual-playback leg of motion-continuity and delivery continuity has no artefact and no named viewing route; check.py's scope says it does not judge animation.", "correction": "Reword consumers-normal-motion to what the checker asserts; keep 'wall-clock not measured'; name caller viewing of the live page under normal motion (1x and 3x) as the route for the playback leg, recorded as a visual observation. Three legs stay separate: frameMs constant (mechanical), frame-index arithmetic (mechanical), actual playback (visual/temporal).", "locators": ["sv-live-sample", "sc-live-single", "sc-timeline", "sc-scope"]}

{"id": "C11", "severity": "clarify", "criteria": ["successor-01.working.q.frame-assembly"], "field": "sources / basis", "finding": "Raised by the specialist (S3) and verified by the caller: the frame-selection/assembly policy obligation is stated in AUTHORING-STAGE.md lines 31-32, which the proposal's 33-entry source index omits; FOCUSED-SUCCESSOR lines 40-43 authorise reuse and forbid invented observations but do not state an assembly policy.", "correction": "Add AUTHORING-STAGE.md (sha256 in this file's source index) and cite lines 31-32 for the assembly clause; keep lines 40-43 for reuse authorisation.", "locators": ["stage-assembly", "assign-step4-reuse"]}

{"id": "C12", "severity": "note", "criteria": ["successor-01.working.q.live-preference-switch", "successor-01.working.q.reduced-motion-consumer-mapping"], "field": "check vs checker support", "finding": "Raised by the specialist (S12) and verified by the caller: check.py's [switch] block inspects only running cells (line 180), so 'other states repaint unchanged' is unasserted; the phase map (lines 67-69) has no expected motion for an as-launched forced-reduced run, so the startup-preference route named in the evidence_route is unasserted.", "correction": "Add the two assertions to the checker at production time, or label those clauses as caller visual observations on the reduced-phase screenshot. No change to the required outcome.", "locators": ["sc-switch-running-only", "sc-phase-map", "cap-phases"]}

